<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Surkh Kotal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Surkh Kotal is an archaeological site in Baghlan Province, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, where a hilltop dynastic sanctuary of the Kushan kings stood. French archaeologists excavated it from 1952, uncovering monumental stairways, royal statues and a long inscription in Bactrian written in Greek script, which was key to understanding the Kushans' language.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/surkh-kotal.jpg" alt="Surkh Kotal" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Afghanistan in the Early 1960s · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Staircase,_Surkh_Kotal,_2%E2%80%934_century_CE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
